window.ENECS_CONTENT=window.ENECS_CONTENT||{};window.ENECS_CONTENT.en={"2781":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>PROVISORIUM KINDERGARTEN SCHWEFEL</strong> <strong>FUNCTIONAL</strong> The temporary kindergarten Schwefel in Vaduz was planned and realized in eight months. Due to the local conditions with already elaborated superstructure plans, which are still in the approval phase, boundary and building distances as well as a landslide danger zone, the solution with containers was very difficult. For lighting, the building received very few, but very large windows. The desire for low-lying windows, which would give the kindergarteners direct access and visual contact to the outside space, could unfortunately only be fulfilled in the entrance area due to the danger of landslides.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>FUNCTIONAL</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Copyright-Angaben © Ralph Feiner</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-187-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1512,"h":849},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-71-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-146-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-182-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1560,"h":876},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-251-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2086,"h":1392},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-323-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2201,"h":1469},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Siegbert Kranz Architektur AG</strong> <strong>SOLAR DIRECT GAIN HOUSE</strong> This two-apartment house is located in Balzers in the Principality of Liechtenstein. The envelope of facade and roof surfaces should form a unity as far as possible. With the roof covering of Eternit and the dark wooden facade, this design expression was achieved. The south side of the roof was completely covered with Sunskin roof photovoltaic modules. In order to maintain a similar structure of the PV modules, the north side was covered with Integral Plan. Sustainability is very important to the architect couple Josua and Monika Gamper from Siegbert Kranz Architektur AG, who are also the building owners. Therefore, the house is a solar direct gain house without central heating, which is heated only with the lump wood stove on winter days with little sun.<br> <strong>Copyright-Angaben © Ralph Feiner</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Siegbert Kranz Architektur AG</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>SOLAR DIRECT GAIN HOUSE</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-008-.jpg","alt":"","w":1457,"h":972},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-010.jpg","alt":"","w":720,"h":1080},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-013.jpg","alt":"","w":720,"h":1080},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-017.jpg","alt":"","w":1457,"h":972},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-027-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1707},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-luftbild.jpg","alt":"","w":2304,"h":1534}],"2734":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Ferienhaus Maescha</strong> <strong>Oasis of well-being for the whole family</strong> With the construction of the vacation home in the hamlet of Masescha at 1250 m.a.s.l., the family has fulfilled a dream. A soothing house in a special place was created. The vacation house is situated gently on the slope with a gable on the valley side, as is customary in the area. The fantastic view into the valley and the Liechtenstein and Swiss mountains captivates everyone.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Ferienhaus Maescha</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Copyright-Angaben © Michael Zanghellini, Anja Meier-Eberle</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-187-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1512,"h":849},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-71-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-146-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-182-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1560,"h":876},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-251-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2086,"h":1392},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-323-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2201,"h":1469},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Wertstoffsammelstelle Schaan</strong> On behalf of the municipality of Schaan, a roof was built for the existing recycling collection point. The openwork structure lends the building lightness and airiness despite its imposing dimensions. The design follows the wood-friendly construction, the form completely follows the function. The building, which has a signal effect for regional value creation and sustainability, demonstrates the power of local trade and resources. The building becomes a positive image carrier for the client (municipality) and at the same time for sustainable timber construction.<br> <strong>Copyright-Angaben © Michael Zanghellini</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Wertstoffsammelstelle Schaan</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-008-.jpg","alt":"","w":1457,"h":972},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-010.jpg","alt":"","w":720,"h":1080},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-013.jpg","alt":"","w":720,"h":1080},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-017.jpg","alt":"","w":1457,"h":972},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-027-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1707},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/wh-balzers-luftbild.jpg","alt":"","w":2304,"h":1534}],"2658":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>MFH St. Wolfgang, Triesen</strong> An environmentally friendly heat pump heating system, which extracts the heat requirement from underground by means of geothermal probes / groundwater, ensures low energy and maintenance costs. The insulation values of the individual components meet the requirements of the new energy ordinance.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>MFH St. Wolfgang, Triesen</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Copyright-Angaben © <strong>Oliver Jaist</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-187-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1512,"h":849},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-71-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-146-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-182-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1560,"h":876},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-251-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2086,"h":1392},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-323-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2201,"h":1469}],"2654":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Beitrag zur Biodiversitätaaa</strong> I can fully identify with the overall result achieved by our experienced team and the qualified construction experts, and that it absolutely meets my expectations,” shares the business owner and builder Helmut Verling with satisfaction. The architect and home designer is also pleased with the feedback he receives from external parties. “One small but important detail is particularly often addressed: the planting and design of the outdoor space. It was important to us to give as many different native plants as possible a place in the greenery and thus to make our contribution to biodiversity.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Beitrag zur Biodiversitätaaa</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Copyright-Angaben © Daniel Schwendener</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-187-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1512,"h":849},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-71-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-146-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-182-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1560,"h":876},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-251-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2086,"h":1392},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-323-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2201,"h":1469}],"2384":[{"t":"h","html":"BSV Srl"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Contact</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"BSV Srl<br> Via Covelano, 48<br> I-39028 Silandro (BZ) – South Tyrol"},{"t":"p","html":"Phone +39 0473 876 200"},{"t":"p","html":"info@bsv.bz<br> <a href=\"https://www.bsv.bz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.bsv.bz</a><br> <a href=\"https://www.designline07.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.designline07.com</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Variety and vision</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Individual solutions, personal guidance, innovative technologies and outstanding quality have been the hallmarks of the company BSV for decades."},{"t":"p","html":"Our windows made of wood, timber-aluminium or UPVC-aluminium set standards and put every room in the right light. They are complemented by our wide range of high-quality doors for which we select the right elements for every interior and exterior from a wide range of colours, shapes and materials. In single rooms or complete buildings, individual and technically high-quality sun shading solutions ensure the right climate. The frameless glazing and large sliding elements of our Designline07 brand are the perfect example of a design that is both functional and stylish."},{"t":"p","html":"We strive constantly for new, innovative solutions to make every building project unique and believe that the best ideas and solutions emerge from mutual trust and open communication, in keeping with our motto: Building on trust."},{"t":"p","html":"Photos ©"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/04-BSV-Villa-Passau-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1440},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/03-BSV-Villa-Passau-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1440},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/06-BSV-Villa-Passau-1-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1441},{"t":"p","html":"Villa Passau"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/01-BSV-Villa-Neuenstadt-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1707},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/02-BSV-Villa-Neuenstadt-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1707},{"t":"p","html":"Villa Neuenstadt"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/09-BSV-Wohnhaus-Buchen-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1707},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/08-BSV-Wohnhaus-Buchen-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1707},{"t":"p","html":"Residential house Buchen"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/12-BSV-Antonianum-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1707},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/11-BSV-Antonianum-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1715},{"t":"p","html":"Antonianum"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/07-BSV-Wohnhaus-Laas-1.jpg","alt":"","w":2217,"h":2244},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/10-BSV-Ferienhaus-Lago-Maggiore.jpg","alt":"","w":1831,"h":1373},{"t":"p","html":"Residential building Laas and vacation home Lago Maggiore"}],"2327":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Technical College for Construction “Peter Anich” in Bolzano</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"The original school building dates back to 1980. The content of the order was the energetic refurbishment and the redesign of the entrance and administration area. This construction task made it possible to redesign the outer shell and essential interior spaces of the building. The material and colour design was coordinated with the existing context of the surrounding schools and the nearby natural landscape. In the design of the interior spaces, a new colour concept and additional transparency between the rooms were realised to create an inviting ambience."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Fotos: © René Riller</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-187-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1512,"h":849},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-71-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-146-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-182-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1560,"h":876},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-251-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2086,"h":1392},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-323-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2201,"h":1469}],"2321":[{"t":"h","html":"Architekturbüro Martin Stecher<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Schönthaler shows what building ecology can do</strong> Concrete paving blocks, concrete blocks, concrete piles for orchards, concrete iron processing, custom and custom-made prefabricated concrete parts, New Jersey concrete guide walls, cellar shafts, hemp acoustic panels, formwork articles, prefabricated ceilings. These are just a few of the many building materials that the local construction industry sources from Schönthaler. Less well known, at least in non-specialist circles, is the ecological side that Schönthaler is continuously developing and consistently expanding. The natural material hemp fascinated business owner Martin Schönthaler years ago: “Processing it into hemp bricks for the building industry was an important milestone for the development of the company and our production site in Eyrs. The ecological footprint in building construction can be significantly improved with co2 neutral hemp.”<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Fotos: © René Riller</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-187-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1512,"h":849},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-71-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-146-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2207,"h":1473},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-182-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":1560,"h":876},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-251-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2086,"h":1392},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/202219114ProvKindergartenSchwefel-323-HDR-Copy.jpg","alt":"","w":2201,"h":1469}],"2281":[{"t":"p","html":"#SCHOOL AS A HOUSE FOR CHILDREN The Gais primary school is part of a competition project to redesign the village centre of Gais. With the conversion and extension of the school, as well as the conversion and extension of the town hall, a cultural centre for the community was to be created.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"#SCHOOL AS A HOUSE FOR CHILDREN"},{"t":"p","html":"Foto <strong>©</strong>Oliver Jaist"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/04-BSV-Villa-Passau-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1440},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/03-BSV-Villa-Passau-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1440},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/06-BSV-Villa-Passau-1-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1441},{"t":"p","html":"Villa Passau"},{"t":"h","html":"Residential and commercial building Pertinger, Mühlbach"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>WOHN und GESCHÄFTSHAUS PERTINGER, Mühlbach</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"In the middle of Mühlbach stands an old craftsman’s house. It is the house of a cobbler. It nestles against the the old cemetery wall, and together with its neighbouring house the entrance to the historic shopping street Katharina Lanz. The simple house of yesterday no longer exists. Over the years, many fashions have been over the years. We are tearing down the house. It’s not the house that’s important, but the house as part of a coherent of a harmonious ensemble of houses at the foot of the church. houses at the foot of the church. We let a new house grow. We continue to build on the ensemble. We build in today, with respect for yesterday. The cobbler stays in the village. So he can still live and work in the centre work in the centre. We hope for the spark that will ignite in the alley. in the alley. For the good of the village."},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/02_134_ER_161203_Pertinger_0056_FU_%C2%A9_Jaist.jpg","alt":"","w":2000,"h":1500},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/24_134_ER_170207_Pertinger_0309_FU_%C2%A9_Jaist-scaled.jpg","alt":"","w":2560,"h":1713},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/31_134_ER_161203_Pertinger_0005_FU_%C2%A9_Jaist.jpg","alt":"","w":1334,"h":1000},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/20_134_ER_161203_Pertinger_0239_FU_%C2%A9_Jaist.jpg","alt":"","w":1500,"h":1003}],"1411":[{"t":"h","html":"Architectural office<br>Margareta Schwarz"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“Building with straw in South Tyrol – Dietrichhof a bsunders Platzl”.</strong> For “farm vacations” four vacation apartments in straw construction were realized at the Dietrichhof in Feldthurns, with a net area of about 30 m2 each. The old barn had a wooden structure with a roof worth preserving. Therefore, the idea arose to place the vacation apartments as round pavilions – only plastered – freestanding in the existing barn shell, which protects against wind and weather.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © studio margareta schwarz"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1380":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Winery Bolzano</strong> The realized new building of the Bolzano Winery is the architectural result of an intensive examination of the functional necessities of energy-saving and quality-preserving wine production “in free fall”.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Winery Bolzano</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Ivo Corrà"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1451":[{"t":"p","html":"Carbon is the basis of all life – and in the form of CO2 a major problem for the climate. Only a small part of the carbon is in the air. Much larger carbon reservoirs are forests, soils or oceans. In one cubic meter of construction timber, almost one ton of CO2 is permanently stored. Wood is therefore the ideal material for climate-positive construction. A house made of solid wood is a great natural carbon store. One such storage facility is located in Verdistraße in Brixen. The diocese of Bolzano-Bressanone has realized there a residential house made of solid wood in the “Klimahaus A Nature Standard”.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Photos: ©</strong>Barbara Obkircher"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Vivius-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1100,"h":733},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Vivius-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1100,"h":733},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Vivius-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1100,"h":733},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Vivius-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1100,"h":733},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Vivius-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1100,"h":733},{"t":"p","html":"Solid wood house Bressanone"}],"1435":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Contact</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"fides interiors of the Jakob Meraner<br> Pillhof 85<br> 39057 Appiano – South Tyrol"},{"t":"p","html":"Phone +39 349 213 08 13<br> info@fides.bz.it<br> <a href=\"https://www.fides.bz.it/de\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.fides.bz.it</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>High quality, sophisticated and efficient</strong><br> <strong>Planning, equipment, implementation, turnkey handover</strong> fides, trust. Nothing is more valuable than that. If you are thinking of redesigning your living space, you want your wishes to be respected and your money to be well invested. At fides interiors, creative minds leave no stone unturned in transforming customers’ needs, desires and living ideas into a holistic design concept. The planning allows to feel the greatest responsibility towards the site, nature and people who will live in the object. This means: interior design with high-quality, natural materials such as wood, metal and stone. Coherent lighting concepts that are highly energy efficient. Equipment for the kitchen at the most innovative technical level. Whether new construction, conversion or renovation: fides interiors creates unique projects, developed in close teamwork.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Meraner &amp; Hauser, BZ<br> <a href=\"https://meraner-hauser.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.meraner-hauser.com</a>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1455":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ONE FOR ALL. ALL FOR YOUR CONSTRUCTION PROJECT.</strong> arcFACTORY – the merger of four successful craft enterprises – is your specialist for turnkey construction, professional renovation and energetic refurbishment in South Tyrol. <strong>Contact:</strong> arcFACTORY<br> Bahnhofstraße 4<br> I-39040 Tramin an der Weinstraße (BZ) Tel. +39 0471 1726615<br> Fax. +39 0471 1703151 info@arcfactory.eu<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Contact:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"info@arcfactory.eu"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © ?"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1474":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Contact</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Architetto Marco Sette</strong><br> Via Negrelli 8<br> 39100 Bolzano-Italy<br> ph. +39 0471 1813654<br> m. +39 339 5936660<br> info@m-7.it"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Casa Salute</strong> <strong>DE – New seat “CASA SALUTE” in Margreid<br></strong><strong>Winner of CasaClima Awards 2014</strong> The challenge of the construction task consisted in the realization of a building with near-natural materials, which on the one hand, based on the solid wood wall “ONLY WOOD” uses neither dowels nor glues and at the same time also functions as a plus energy building based on high energy efficiency (Klimahaus Gold Nature and Passivhaus), the whole with appealing and fresh architecture. Energy efficient buildings often show great similarities in design and appearance, with high attention to energy efficiency and less to the design aspects.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Casa Salute</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © M7 Architecture+Design"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Villa ###lt##br##gt##126"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Villa 126</strong> Foreword EG The design development of the new building is based on the client’s desire to create a low-energy, healthy and sustainable construction, suitable for becoming a permanent residence with two separate units. Wood was chosen as the main construction material. The intrinsic characteristics of the material and the proximity to the lake, with possible flooding, determine the need to provide a reinforced concrete raised floor as a base for the building. The size and internal position of the lot in the whole neighborhood, with the proximity of several neighboring buildings, determines a binding situation in the planimetric distribution. Taking advantage of the possibility of positioning the new building on the site of the existing one, even if within the buffer zone, the project tries to keep the land as free as possible from construction in favor of green space.<br> Photos © M7 Architecture+Design"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Villa 126</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Foreword EG"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Villa-126-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Villa-126-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800}],"1416":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Aslago Zanchi</strong> <strong>Contact</strong> Area architetti associati<br> Via Castel Flavon 37c<br> 39100 Bolzano Tel: +39 0471 301648<br> Fax +39 0471 051349<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Aslago Zanchi</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Contact</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Tel: +39 0471 301648<br> Fax +39 0471 051349"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Ivo Corra"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Camping Merano<br>Holzner"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Samuel Holzner"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"h","html":"Casa<br>Concordia"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Concordia"}],"1415":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Water Wall Condominium, St. Anton Bolzano</strong> Klimahaus A” was planned according to building biology criteria and, as far as possible, executed in this way: Wood-concrete composite ceiling, low-temperature heating, solar system for water heating, gas condensing boiler, extensively greened roof.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Rene Riller"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1410":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Babioshof</strong> Babios – nature, emotions, vacation On the building site in the middle of the vineyards of Kaltern, a closed farmstead with vacation apartments for farm vacations was planned. The private area of the young farming family, which has been active in agriculture for several generations, is housed in a two-story residential building. To the north of this, four vacation apartments find space in another structure, which is connected to the private building by a farm store. The apartments are named “löm” (light), ega (water), tera (earth) and aria (air), named by the 4 elements, without which the work in and with nature would be unthinkable.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Babioshof</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Babios – nature, emotions, vacation"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Thomas Alessandri Photography"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Ansitz###lt##br&gt;Hörtenberg"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Ansitz Hörtenberg</strong> The construction of the Hörtenberg manor in its present form as a Renaissance residence dates back to the end of the 16th century. Due to various interventions in the previous decades, the generous, regular division of the floor plan was interrupted by the division into smaller units (apartments). A guiding principle of the project was to carry out a deconstruction, to free the building fabric from the subsequently inserted interior partition walls and thus to expose the stately rooms again. Thus, a noble city hotel could be created in a central location, where historically valuable building substance meets modern architecture.<br> Photos © Giovanni De Sandre"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Ansitz Hörtenberg</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Giovanni De Sandre"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Villa-126-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Villa-126-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Villa 126"}],"1404":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residential complex Schönblick Vilpian</strong> We are not building for the feuilleton, but for the future of our children.<br> The construction task was to create a housing estate for 19 local families on the site of an abandoned lodging establishment. The goal was to create a high-quality yet affordable living environment through energy-efficient design and thoughtful planning decisions and construction details. The building envelope complies with the climate house standard A-Nature ( approx. 21 kWh/m²a). Solar collectors on the roof for water heating, an air-source heat pump for basic heating requirements via low-temperature heating, rainwater infiltration, constructive sun protection and decentralized residential ventilation round off the sustainable construction method.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Lukas Abram"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Residential house###lt##br&gt;Drususstrasse"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residential house Drususstrasse</strong> We like this project because it shows how valuable living space can be created with sensible upcycling and redensification, even in difficult urbanistic situations.<br> In the midst of a densely built urban context, an old hotel stands empty on a busy street. Due to the location and the lack of expansion possibilities, operation as a HDThe entire building has been energy upgraded and complies with climate house standard B. For this purpose, the existing balconies were demolished, thus preventing possible thermal bridges. The floor slab, which mostly rested on the ground, was insulated, and all exterior walls and roof surfaces were insulated. The windows were replaced with energy-saving otel no longer useful. Therefore, the building is to be converted into a residential building.<br> Photos © Alexa Rainer"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residential house Drususstrasse</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Alexa Rainer"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1394":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>GREEN ROOF</strong> Modern fruit farm in South Tyrol Rarely in South Tyrol a farm is built completely from scratch and even more rarely in this size. Surrounded by orchards, the two-winged structure combines economic and residential areas of a modern fruit farm under a green roof. Great importance is attached to ecologically sustainable architecture made of natural building materials such as larch wood, concrete and plaster.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>GREEN ROOF</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Modern fruit farm in South Tyrol"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Günther Neumair"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Steep<br>template"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Steep template</strong><br> <strong>CONSTRUCTION MATERIAL LIGHT</strong> Energetic renovation and extension of residential house in Lana An energy-efficient extension (ZK-BL) The energy-efficient building is heated by the air-source heat pump. This also provides the necessary cooling in summer. The generous window areas not only provide plenty of natural light, but also solar heat gains in the winter. In summer, the installed vertical awnings serve for the necessary thermal protection. “Architecture is the artful, correct, and grand play of structures gathered under the light.”<br> Le Corbusier<br> Photos © Günther Neumair"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Architecture is the artful, correct, and grand play of structures gathered under the light.”<br> Le Corbusier"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1393":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Project: Baur</strong> The aim of the design was to work out a unified concept for the two residential volumes. The sensitive embedding in the steep terrain was another important point of the concept. The main elements of the design basically consist of three bodies, which differ in their materiality. The building was constructed in climate house standard B.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Project: Baur</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Project<br>Zingerle"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Zingerle</strong> The project provides for the construction of a new granny annexe and energy renovation of the existing building. Applying the energy bonus for existing buildings, the entire volume is brought up to climate house standard C. The new volume was deliberately formulated as an independent body, but in part picks up characteristics of the existing building; among other things, the shape of the monopitch roof and the materiality of the wooden attic.<br> Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Zingerle</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1392":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Alpenrose Wellness</strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos ©"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1391":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Interior Tower</strong> <strong>A project by architect Stefan Klement, in collaboration with Martin Hilpold</strong> In the immediate vicinity of the Brixen Nord freeway exit is the Forch 2 commercial zone, where the “Interior Tower” is currently being built. This is a building complex that brings together diverse trades of related industries in one place. Individual companies that appeal to similar customer groups can work together to increase their appeal. Specifically, these are the areas: Building Furnishings, Plumbing and Lighting, which will be represented in the “Interior Tower” in the future. What appears visually separate on the outside is in many cases connected on the inside.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Interior Tower</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Raymotion and Stefan Klement"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1390":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“Casa” Vera Weiss</strong> Originally, the apartment was the workshop of a craftsman. It was especially important to retain the old and breathe new life into it. Thus, the old credenza finds its new place in a modern, spacious ambience. A special highlight is the jungle wallpaper, on which the color concept is based. In this apartment there are many hidden rooms and storage space, so some rooms are even hidden from visitors.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“Casa” Vera Weiss</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © DPerbellini &amp; Luca Photos"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1370":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>House Gasser</strong> In Lüsen, a village about 20 minutes’ drive from Brixen in South Tyrol, a concrete sculpture sits confidently in the landscape. By expanding the existing residential units, the developers were not only able to create space for the younger generation, but also breathe new life into the building.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>House Gasser</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Samuel Holzner"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1383":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Simmlerhof</strong><br> <strong>Redevelopment – Revitalization Simmlerhof (listed building)</strong> However, the primary goal is also to create a more adequate habitability of the farmhouse for the owner and his family. For this purpose, the building is to be appropriately renovated and maintained in the area of the residential building. In order to mitigate the cold and drafts in the house, thermal insulation measures are planned above all on the upper floors, as well as the renovation of the windows and doors. The choice of building materials plays an essential role. Environmentally compatible building and living means, above all, dealing sensitively and sustainably with the existing building fabric.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Oskar Messner"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1382":[{"t":"h","html":"Studio<br>Hannes Denicolò"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Chalet mountain friend</strong> Traditional cottage atmosphere meets contemporary architecture.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Chalet mountain friend</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos ©"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1367":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>House MIT –</strong>reconstruction and extension residential house with energy renovation. The MIT house is an extension of a residential building with energy renovation and construction of an additional apartment for urban densification. The extension in timber construction transforms the existing building into a contemporary structure and blends harmoniously into the context thanks to natural materials such as the wooden façade in larch. The new penthouse apartment is characterized by generous glazing and an extensive roof terrace, which, together with the ecological construction method, ensure a high quality of living.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos ©"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Loft <br>P"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Loft P</strong> <strong>Construction of a loft in the former tool shed in the course of the revitalization of the farmstead P</strong> As part of the revitalization of an existing farm site, a loft with an open, generously lit living space was added to the existing equipment building. In this, in turn, a cube in solid wood construction was inserted, in a sense as a “house within a house”. It accommodates the kitchen in addition to the shower, children’s room, stairs on the first level and open parent’s room and bathroom on the second level. The light glazed wooden surfaces give the body the necessary lightness in the light-flooded loft.<br> Photos ©"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Loft-P-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Loft-P-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Loft-P.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933}],"1363":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>KINDERGARTEN SCHLUDERNS</strong> Child-friendly and sustainable: With the Schluderns kindergarten, Roland Baldi Architects realized a wooden building with a gable roof, plastered facade and significant, differently sized windows, which with their staggered arrangement and dimension are reminiscent of an oversized children’s drawing. Inside, all rooms are accessed via the spacious, light-filled foyer, which is also a welcome, recreation and play area.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>KINDERGARTEN SCHLUDERNS</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Oskar Da Riz"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Civil defense center<br>Ritten"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Civil defense center Ritten</strong> Saving architecture, stamped out of concrete: With the new building of the Civil Defense Center Ritten, Roland Baldi Architects have built a joint home for the fire department, the mountain rescue service and the White Cross, which creates cross-competence conditions for smooth operations. The two-story structure, built as Klimahaus A, was integrated into the natural course of the terrain and communicates with the main street running there and the residential zone behind it via the north-facing entrance area. Most of the volume, however, was arranged in a compact structure below the parking lot.<br> Photos © Oskar Da Riz"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1353":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>AMOLARIS Private Garden Chalets &amp; Residence</strong> The task was to build 8 chalets and a small restaurant to extend the former Residence Obermühle (founded in 1970). In addition to the given architectural goals, it was also a concern of the client to implement an ecological and natural construction method. Together with executing companies, which come exclusively from South Tyrol, a high-quality and energy-efficient object could be built.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Photos: ©Klaus</strong>Peterlin"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1352":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>The Rubner farm</strong> Peter Rubner runs a farm in the municipality of Kiens in South Tyrol. In a fantastic location. With one foot integrated in the village structure, with the other foot in the green.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>The Rubner farm</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Hitthaler_Rubner"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Villa<br>Paola"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Villa Paola</strong> A small villa stands in a relatively large garden. The owners of the villa decide to sell part of the garden. The construction company Puntel acquires the property and commissions us with the planning. The location of the property is very interesting. It is located a few steps away from the center and yet you can live there like in a small garden settlement. This also shows that we are often asked where this house with the curved balconies is actually located: in the middle of Bruneck and you can’t find it.<br> Photos © wisthaler.com"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © wisthaler.com"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1362":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Apartment house Parc Hotel Sulden</strong> The appearance of the new building fits into the typical for this area – small hamlet structure with individually conditioned building orientations, details and characteristics. The architectural characteristics of these buildings will be characterized mainly by the materials, the appropriate details and by the spatial and functional requirements of the construction task: Guest apartments with the outdoor areas in the form of terraces on the upper floors (upper floor and first floor 2) in wooden construction. Company apartments, reception areas, ancillary rooms on the lower floors (first floor 2 / first floor 1) realized in solid construction (reinforced concrete and masonry) with a surface adapted to the local building tradition, such as mineral plaster or stone surfaces.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Apartment house Parc Hotel Sulden</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Samuel Holzner"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Local area design###lt##br&gt;Schlanders 2020"},{"t":"p","html":"The project for the new village square with inn in Covelano is part of the competition “Ortsraumgestaltung Schlanders 2020”, which was won in 2014. One of the areas covered was Covelano, a fraction of the municipality of Silandro, located a little off the main roads but directly on the national network of cycle paths. Covelano has its own marble quarry, the Covelano marble, which is very profitable for the village and which the village community is rightly proud of. The competition area in Covelano included an ensemble-protected central area with an old fire station with forecourt as a maneuvering area, but which had been unused for more than 20 years.<br> Photos © Samuel Holzner"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"},{"t":"h","html":"Residence###lt##br&gt;Winzerhöhe"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residence Winzerhöhe</strong> “How to deal with an existing building whose architectural qualities turn out to be rather modest and whose stylistic execution no longer meets the expectations; what can be realized with the given budget and how to succeed in developing a clear, harmonious and contemporary concept for a new operation with the given framework conditions.” These were the questions faced by builders and planners at the start of the project. The planning was preceded by many discussions and a thorough analysis of the existing situation, at some point it was clear what was wanted, now it was up to the architects to find tools to turn these ideas into reality.<br> Photos © Benjamin Pfitscher"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residence Winzerhöhe</strong>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“How to deal with an existing building whose architectural qualities turn out to be rather modest and whose stylistic execution no longer meets the expectations; what can be realized with the given budget and how to succeed in developing a clear, harmonious and contemporary concept for a new operation with the given framework conditions.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Benjamin Pfitscher"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Concordia"},{"t":"h","html":"Residential house###lt##br&gt;Ofenbaur"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residential house Ofenbaur</strong> The existing Gasthof Ofenbaur will be demolished and subsequently a terraced residential complex will be realized. Architectural Concept Terrace Housing: Due to the ideal nature of the existing slope formation, the idea for this project was to apply the concept of terrace housing. With terracing, the building volumes can be gently embedded into the natural terrain following the current slope. The terracing offers the advantage that all residential units have a spacious terrace in front.<br> Photos © Alexa Rainer"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residential house Ofenbaur</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Alexa Rainer"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933}],"1343":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>House Barbian</strong> The semi-detached house is situated on a small and very narrow plot. The height difference of the terrain is two and a half stories between the entrance area with the garage and the natural terrain at the back of the building. That is why the house develops upwards in mezzanines. A glazed recess illuminates the centrally located stairwell and provides access to the individual levels. Also above the staircase, a large horizontal window provides natural lighting from above. Only the rooms and bathrooms are separated with doors, the rest is a single public space with different functions and living spaces on each level. Thus, the house gets a strong reference to the outdoor space with views and small open spaces.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>House Barbian</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Jürgen Eheim"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1345":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residence P.</strong> During planning, great attention was paid to a natural integration of the building into the natural terrain. On a slope above the promenade that leads from Oberbozen to Lichtenstern lies the residential house with an imposing view of the Rosengarten. The residential house was built in the climate house A – standard.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residence P.</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Anneliese Kompatscher"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1355":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hotel Plunhof</strong> The Wellness Hotel Plunhof is located in Ridnaun near Sterzing. The 4-star superior hotel is managed by the Volgger family, composed of eight siblings and mother Paula, under the motto “Home of the generations” is one of the most renowned wellness hotels in South Tyrol. In addition, the hotel has an EU Ecolabel certification and a climate hotel pre-certification, which will be completed in the course of the realization of the next construction lot, which is currently being planned. The architectural design of the conversion focuses on two themes: The connection to the centuries-old mining tradition of the location, which was implemented through the choice of materials and the integration of targeted design elements, as well as the connection to nature through the large-scale window elements with flowing transitions between inside and outside, as well as unique panoramic views of the mountains of Ridnaun.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hotel Plunhof</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Hotel Plunhof"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Office community###lt##br&gt;Planwerk"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Office partnership Planwerk</strong> The headquarters of the office community Planwerk.it is the result of close cooperation between five technical freelancers in the district of Sterzing. The design of the single-story building emphasizes an open, bright environment for daily work and collaboration.<br> Facts / Figures:<br> Client: Bürogemeinschaft Planwerk.it : Arch. Bastian Helfer – Ing. Gianluca Cordani – Arch.int. Kurt Eisendle – Geom. Jürgen Salzburger – Ing. Artur Braunhofer<br> Year of manufacture: 2019-2020<br> Climate house class: A<br> Photos © Bastian Helfer"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Office partnership Planwerk</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Bastian Helfer"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Loft-P-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Loft-P-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Loft-P.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Loft P"}],"1342":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Cirna – Gentle Luxury Logdes</strong><br> <strong>The concept</strong> To convey exquisite vacation moments, moments that remain in memory and give pleasure, to offer their guests exactly the space and comfort that each individual needs for themselves to gather new energies, that is the goal that the Linter family, which already runs the Apartments Schwarzlehen in the second generation, has set itself. Unique, natural and full of strength as it is the natural landscape that surrounds the “Cirna”, so should be the vacation that the guest spends in the new lodges of the family. Values such as independence, freedom, restraint, down-to-earthness and sustainability are the supporting pillars in the family members’ personal dealings with each other and with their guests.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Photos: © Rene</strong>Riller"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1337":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Bar Lions Mals</strong> Löwen Bar, welcoming, elegant and immersed in an atmosphere of the past, becomes the perfect meeting place to relax. A lounge designed to enjoy a drink, where it is important to drink well and feel at home in a space where you can live freely and discover the quality of the precious raw materials of our land and the excellence and design from around the world. The result is a club where areas of different shapes, color schemes and a mix of materials and finishes offer flexible comfort and a recognizable, welcoming and familiar place.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Bar Lions Mals</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos ©"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"H&amp;T##lt##br##gt###"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>H&amp;T</strong> The single-family house in Mals (BZ) inspires with its special location and the holistic conception.The fantastic view of the Ortler mountains in combination with the consistent design creates a home with the highest design standards. From one source and without compromise. Like a red thread, the overall atmosphere runs through all rooms of the house and perfectly reflects the personality and lifestyle of the owners. Inspiration and design guideline of this object is the play with surfaces, natural shapes and reduced lines – wood, lacquer, metal, stone and glass in combination create the extravagant overall image.<br> Photos ©"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>H&amp;T</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1321":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Symbiosis of architecture and ecology –</strong><strong>House Tasser-Nocker at the “Unterhuberhof” in Reischach (Bruneck)</strong> During the planning phase, several variants were played out in a goal-oriented dialogue – “ping-pong” – until it was possible to decide on the final room program, the construction method and the materiality. The originally planned “pure” wooden house became a wooden post and beam building with clay brick infill and clay plaster.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Photos: ©</strong>Silver Salt Fabian Haspinger/Caroline Renzler"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1338":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Alphotel Tyrol</strong> <strong>CLOSE TO NATURE – REGIONAL – SUSTAINABLE</strong> The architecture makes use of natural materials. Wood and stone are the main actors of the design and form a unity with the surrounding landscape. Other natural materials such as clay, wool and glass are determinants of the overall design. The wood used comes from the valley. Built in traditional wooden construction and covered with typical local “shingles”, the forest chalets live up to their name.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Alphotel Tyrol</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Architects Haller &amp; Ohnewein"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"HOFST###lt##br&gt;”DITLKRAMER”"},{"t":"p","html":"Tradition, naturalness and spirit of renewal characterize the architectural image of the farm. The Integration into the surrounding landscape and the new purpose of the farmstead determine the design. Efficient energy use and the resulting living comfort play a decisive role in the implementation of the new farmstead.<br> Photos © Architects Haller &amp; Ohnewein"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"},{"t":"h","html":"WOHNKOMPLEX##lt##br##gt###OLYMPIA"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>RESIDENTIAL COMPLEX “OLYMPIA</strong> <strong>A SYMBIOSIS OF STRAIGHT AND SWEEPING</strong> In the middle of Sterzing you can find the housing estate OLYMPIA. Very thoughtful and subtle, the design language of the building stands out from the surrounding residential buildings. A symbiosis of straight and sweeping lines draw a memorable design and determine the appearance<br> Photos © Architects Haller &amp; Ohnewein"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>RESIDENTIAL COMPLEX “OLYMPIA</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Concordia"},{"t":"h","html":"Service building###lt##br&gt;Kreuzbergpass"},{"t":"p","html":"Client: Community of Sesto Place: Sesto / South Tyrol<br> Cubature: 412 m³<br> Project and realization: 2019-2020<br> Photos: Gustav Willeit Competition and project with willeit architecture The concept of the nature park administration foresees the creation of distinctive buildings with recognition value at individual strategically important locations in the “Dolomites UNESCO World Heritage” area. This includes the Kreuzberg Pass, which at 1,636m above sea level is the easternmost gateway to the nature park and an important starting point for numerous hiking tours and other leisure activities in the mountains.<br> Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"p","html":"Client: Community of Sesto"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Residential house Ofenbaur"}],"1395":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hotel Am Sonnenhang</strong><br> <strong>Demolition and reconstruction hotel “Am Sonnenhang</strong> In the center of Dorf Tirol the former hotel “Tirolerhof” was demolished and rebuilt and now forms together with the adjacent residence “Am Sonnenhang” the new hotel residence complex “Am Sonnenhang”. The hotel was certified as a climate house “A”. It is terraced and has large window fronts on the south side. The terraces are arranged in such a way that in summer, when the sun is high, the terraces above guarantee shading and protect against overheating. In winter, on the other hand, the low-lying sun can warm the rooms unhindered and solar gains can be used.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Andreas Stedtler"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1407":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Presulis Lodge</strong> The owners Sylvia Mairhofer and Goller Meinhard had the desire to expand the old inn “Pröslerhof” qualitatively and quantitatively and to create a unique vacation ambience with modern and special vacation apartments. For this purpose, part of the land to the west of the old house was rezoned to a tourism zone.<br> The buildings were designed in climate house standard A and without living space ventilation.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Presulis Lodge</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Hannes Niederkofler"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1340":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Butchery &amp; Enotheque Bernardi</strong> Where once the grain for the old Bruneck hospital was ground, there is now a carefully restored building where, among other things, the bacon of the Bernardi butchery hangs out. The rest of the building was restored to its original design after several reconstructions in the past.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Butchery &amp; Enotheque Bernardi</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Lukas Auer"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Mountain Residence###lt##br&gt;Montana"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Mountain Residence Montana</strong> The Residence Montana is located in a wonderful position on the edge of a small rural settlement in the Val Casies.Over the years, the family business has been repeatedly expanded and modernized. Thus, two older buildings were replaced by a new structure. Spacious apartments, private apartment, foyer, garage and a large panoramic swimming pool was newly built and attached to an existing building. Proportions, materials, choice of colors, roof pitch as well as the embedding in the steeply sloping terrain seek the context to the existing buildings.<br> Photos © Lukas Auer"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Mountain Residence Montana</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"},{"t":"h","html":"Plumbing###lt##br&gt;Messner"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Plumbing Messner</strong> The annex is an extension of the existing premises of the Messner plumbing company. Thanks to the additional cubage, new storage, office and exhibition space could be created. A spacious company apartment has been placed in the attic. A compact and simple structure was docked to the existing building on the street side. The structure reflects the company’s field of activity through the use of sheet metal and metal sheeting.<br> Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Plumbing Messner</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Concordia"},{"t":"h","html":"Residential###lt##br&gt;Cierzo"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residence Cierzo</strong> Next to a large rural building on the valley floor of the Gsiesertal, there is a small residential volume as an extension for the young generation. Out of respect for the tranquil status quo, the proportions, roof pitches, articulation and materials were replicated and reinterpreted in the new building. Despite its smallness, the floor plan conveys a feeling of spaciousness. The simple volume with a high level of detail is a sign of the independence of the new building.<br> Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Residence Cierzo</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Residential house Ofenbaur"},{"t":"h","html":"Apartment ###lt##br##gt##H"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Apartment H</strong> The architecture of the private apartment seeks the play between open sequences of spaces with smooth transitions and areas of retreat. The area of the central kitchen-cum-living-room, complete with piano and a “Schlemme” table, is in direct context with the terrace, which functions as an extended living space in the warmer months of the year. The choice of finishes was consistently reduced to oak wood, black steel, white plaster and doors, and trowelled floors.<br> Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Apartment H</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnung-H-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnung-H-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnung-H-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnung-H-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933}],"1324":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Aparthotel Panorama Living in Meransen</strong> The project envisages a terraced building that is restrainedly transverse to the Slope developed downward in three stages. There is an unobstructed view of the valley to the south from the road above. The part of the building that runs parallel to the slope embeds itself in the terrain and literally disappears into it. The complex is oriented towards the valley, the apartments have for the most part an unobstructed view to the south and towards the Puster Valley.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Hannes Niederkofler"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Hoferhof<br>in Meransen"},{"t":"p","html":"The project envisages the construction of a residential building with a private apartment or 4 vacation apartments and the required agricultural buildings (stable, barn, machine hall, farm store, etc.).<br> Photos © Hannes Niederkofler"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1323":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CAFÉ RESTAURANT CENTRAL</strong> Remodeling &amp; Design Klobenstein am Ritten, 2019 In the course of remodeling and redesigning the aging premises, an inviting and functional inn will be created. To provide the space with more daylight, the existing arched windows on the west and south facades will be opened to the floor and replaced with new glazing. Thus, these facades continue the existing arcade on the north facade of the building. The arched openings on the street-side west façade provide an inviting effect that enlivens the village scene through the increased visual references between the public space and the bar. On the south façade, the generous glazing with wicker awnings extends the restaurant area to include a sunny garden with a wooden terrace, which is now accessible through wooden doors integrated into the sides of the arches.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CAFÉ RESTAURANT CENTRAL</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Oliver Jaist"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"CASA<br>LUIS"},{"t":"p","html":"Klobenstein am Ritten, 2019 Casa Luis is a residence for a young family of six. Their desire for the best views and light, privacy and generous open spaces was as much a design consideration as the morphological nature of the site, sunlight and development guidelines. Neighboring properties are built on to the south and north, and a road runs past the southwest side. Wooded hills, gently sloping meadows and natural stone walls characterize towards the northeast the gentle wide landscape against the background of the mountain panorama of the Dolomites.<br> Photos © Karina Castro"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Karina Castro"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1316":[{"t":"h","html":"Architect ###lt##br##gt##Angelika Mair"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Slope to nature</strong> The building is situated in the middle of a sensitive natural landscape, surrounded by forest and chestnut groves. The log house, built in the 1960-ies, had a size of 170m3. The construction task was to demolish the log house and place a new structure in the garden area. The clients’ aspiration was to treat the garden, which had grown over decades, with care and to create a contemporary living situation.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Slope to nature</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Photos: ©</strong>Angelika Mair"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1339":[{"t":"h","html":"Pedevilla##lt##br##gt##Architects"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Armin-Pedevilla-Alexander-Pedevilla.jpg","alt":"","w":495,"h":400},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Philosophy</strong> “We build with local materials, local craftsmen and the characters of the people who live here. It’s not an intellectual issue, it’s an emotional issue: we want to give our projects the opportunity to age gracefully.” For pedevilla architects, building means consciously dealing with social, cultural, economic and ecological components of everyday life. The integration of a building into existing local structures plays just as important a role as responding to the respective temperature and climate influences. In this context, the issue of consistency becomes an important factor in planning decisions. “We are concerned with the cycles of the materials used, their durability and service life, but also with traditional craftsmanship methods that have been handed down, with knowledge that was thought to be lost; but above all, we are concerned with the fact that materials live.”<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Philosophy</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"ciAsa Aqua ###lt##br##gt###Bad Cortina"},{"t":"p","html":"Client: Aqua Bad Cortina – Alberti Mutschlechner family<br> Place: San Vigilio di Marebbe / South Tyrol<br> Cubature: 920 m³<br> Project and realization: 2018-2019 <strong>“Without insulation – only solid wood from the storm Vaja”.</strong> The ciAsa (Rhaeto-Romanic for house) is a high alpine all-wood residential house in St.Vigil in South Tyrol, surrounded by the Val Badia Dolomites. It stands on a gentle hill, right next to a thermal spring.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"},{"t":"h","html":"Decantei###lt##br&gt;The inn"},{"t":"p","html":"Place: Bressanone/South Tyrol<br> Total area: 800 m² Project and realization: 2018-2019 The new inn is located in the old town of Bressanone in the immediate vicinity of the cathedral. The structural beginnings of the building date back to the 13th century. Among other things, it was the official residence of the cathedral dean. Several successive historic interiors can accommodate up to a hundred people, a courtyard and sunny garden complement the hospitality business.<br> Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"p","html":"Project and realization: 2018-2019"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Casa-Concordia-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Concordia"},{"t":"h","html":"Hotel###lt##br&gt;Bühelwirt"},{"t":"p","html":"Hotel BühelwirtSt. Jakob in Ahrntal / South Tyrol The existing building sits on the Bühel at 1200m above sea level and was extended to the east on the land below. The extension extends over 6 floors and is positioned in the north of the site so as not to restrict the existing structure in its use, in terms of visual relationships and sunlight. The asymmetrically placed gable roof also cleverly plays off the recreational spaces in the existing building and at the same time responds to the urban conditions.<br> Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Wohnhaus-Ofenbaur-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Residential house Ofenbaur"},{"t":"h","html":"Service building###lt##br&gt;Kreuzbergpass"},{"t":"p","html":"Client: Community of Sesto Place: Sesto / South Tyrol<br> Cubature: 412 m³<br> Project and realization: 2019-2020<br> Photos: Gustav Willeit Competition and project with willeit architecture The concept of the nature park administration foresees the creation of distinctive buildings with recognition value at individual strategically important locations in the “Dolomites UNESCO World Heritage” area. This includes the Kreuzberg Pass, which at 1,636m above sea level is the easternmost gateway to the nature park and an important starting point for numerous hiking tours and other leisure activities in the mountains.<br> Photos © Gustav Willeit"},{"t":"p","html":"Client: Community of Sesto"}],"1336":[{"t":"h","html":"Tara##lt##br##gt##Architects"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hotel Saltus</strong> Take a breath, feel relaxation, enjoy the forest and experience grounding – that was the formulated program for the newly built Hotel Saltus in Jenesien near Bolzano. Every single choice of material, every design decision was subordinated to this content-related requirement. And in the end, all the pieces came together to form a coherent whole.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hotel Saltus</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © DPerbellini"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Stadele<br>Rooms"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Stadele Rooms</strong> The Stadele Rooms fits into the village development between Aichweg and Gartenstrasse in Lana as a well-studied fitting piece. Fits and fits perfectly. The building stands there like a monolith of concrete, a monolith that has shaken off all decorative accessories and becomes a piece of jewelry itself. On its bright, velvet surface, climb space-creating dark balcony boxes.<br> Photos © DPerbellini"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"}],"1322":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Prunner Luxury Suites</strong> “With the “Prunner Luxury Suites” project in Schenna, we have realized a synthesis between architecture and rural life, a fused structure between nature and urban space.” UPC – Architects<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Prunner Luxury Suites</strong>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“With the “Prunner Luxury Suites” project in Schenna, we have realized a synthesis between architecture and rural life, a fused structure between nature and urban space.”"},{"t":"p","html":"UPC – Architects"},{"t":"p","html":"Photos © UPC Architects"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}],"1330":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Philosophy</strong> noa* is an award-winning architecture and design studio founded in 2011 by Lukas Rungger and Stefan Rier, based in Bolzano (Italy), Berlin (Germany) and since 2022 also in Milan (Italy). noa* stands for the essential expression of a collaborative work ethic: the young team of architects, designers and artists relies on an interdisciplinary design methodology that is in constant flux depending on the requirements of each project. The concept of “emergence”, where the whole is far more than the sum of its parts, becomes the central strategy of a holistic approach to any design conceived by noa*. <strong>NOA*… THE NETWORK OF INTERNATIONALLY ACTIVE CREATIVE MINDS</strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Philosophy</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"},{"t":"h","html":"Aeon:<br>Where worlds touch each other"},{"t":"p","html":"Boundaries – between past and future, between dream and reality, between inside and outside: noa* makes the invisible lines visible, part of the whole, and above all, instead of a separation, a connection between two worlds.<br> Photo <strong>©</strong>Alex Filz"},{"t":"p","html":"Photo <strong>©</strong>Alex Filz"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/%C2%A9AlexFilz-Floris-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/%C2%A9AlexFilz-Floris-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/%C2%A9AlexFilz-Floris-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/%C2%A9AlexFilz-Floris-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Floris"},{"t":"h","html":"Floris:<br>A park outgrows itself"},{"t":"p","html":"If architecture adopts the vibrancy and diversity of nature, it will never be perceived as a foreign body. noa* has integrated elements for a special hotel project that awaken memories, dreams and perhaps even a bit of a sense of adventure in every guest.<br> Photo <strong>©</strong>Alex Filz"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Camping-Meran-Holzner-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1200,"h":800},{"t":"p","html":"Camping Merano Holzner"},{"t":"h","html":"Lake House<br>Völs"},{"t":"p","html":"It was the famous leap into the deep end: how noa* succeeded with a great deal of flair at the idyllic Völser Weiher lake to tie in with a cherished tradition with a new, modern concept and at the same time harmoniously harmonize architecture with nature.<br> Photo <strong>©</strong>Alex Filz"}],"1315":[{"t":"h","html":"Appropriate"},{"t":"p","html":"The term sustainability is on everyone’s lips – as architects, we bear responsibility in this sense:"},{"t":"p","html":"Design decisions in terms of materiality, form, size, use, flexibility, orientation, social embedding … ideally allow a built environment to emerge that contributes to being able to live and experience the future in a positive way – regardless of scale. Plasma Studio tries in its work – from the design object to the master planning – to appropriately meet site, building task, user and context: there is no recipe for this. With the joy of experimentation, we try to do justice to the future in every project."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Photos: ©</strong>Florian Jaenicke"},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-1.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-2.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-3.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-4.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"img","src":"https://enecs.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dietrichhof-5.jpg","alt":"","w":1400,"h":933},{"t":"p","html":"Dietrichhof"}]};
